Armor of Ro Quests	29	{"kind":"quest","title":"Armor of Ro Quests","wikiPath":"/Armor_of_Ro_Quests","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Temple of Solusek Ro","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Lord Searfire","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Helm of Ro","item":"Helm of Ro","wikiPath":"/Helm_of_Ro"},{"text":"Breastplate of Ro","item":"Breastplate of Ro","wikiPath":"/Breastplate_of_Ro"},{"text":"Vambraces of Ro","item":"Vambraces of Ro","wikiPath":"/Vambraces_of_Ro"},{"text":"Bracer of Ro","item":"Bracer of Ro","wikiPath":"/Bracer_of_Ro"},{"text":"Gauntlets of Ro","item":"Gauntlets of Ro","wikiPath":"/Gauntlets_of_Ro"},{"text":"Greaves of Ro","item":"Greaves of Ro","wikiPath":"/Greaves_of_Ro"},{"text":"Boots of Ro","item":"Boots of Ro","wikiPath":"/Boots_of_Ro"}],"steps":[{"parts":[{"title":"Deepwater Knights"}," (Prexus) (Erudian - ",{"title":"Erudin"},")"],"steps":[{"parts":["The only way to raise faction with the DW knights is to kill ",{"title":"Elial Brook"}," at the docks in Toxxulia Forest. He spawns every 10 minutes. He is a Necro and is often with pet. I also found killing ",{"title":"Aglthin Dasmore"}," and ",{"title":"Noclin Saah"}," does the same thing."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["Once your faction is at Indifferent or Amiable, you can probably start doing quests directly from the Prexus temple.: ",{"title":"Zombie Flesh Quest"}," for facton at Deepwater Knights. This is for the Bracers. ",{"title":"The Estate of Unrest"}," is a good source for this."],"steps":[]},{"parts":[{"title":"Odus Pearls"}," Weligon Steelherder is also looking for Odus Pearls from the Odus harbor. These pearls sit underneath some very easy sharks."],"steps":[]}]},{"parts":[{"title":"Clerics of Underfoot"}," (Brell Serillis) (Dwarven - ",{"title":"Kaladim"},")"],"steps":[{"parts":["The best way to raise Clerics of Underfoot and Miners Guild 249 faction is by bone chips questing. Give bone chips to Gunlok Jure in the Kaladim Paladin guild. This may take a couple hundred bone chips."],"steps":[]}]},{"parts":[{"title":"Clerics of Tunare"}," (Tunare) (High Elf - ",{"title":"Felwithe"},")"],"steps":[{"parts":["Give bone chips to Yeolan Bronzeleaf in the cleric hall of Felwithe. I read it may take 400 bone chips."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["Give muffins to Pandos, a dwarf in West Freeport. You can find Pandos on the 2nd floor of the Hogcallers' Inn."],"steps":[]}]},{"parts":[{"title":"Priests of Life"}," & ",{"title":"Knights of Thunder"}," (Rodcet Nife & Karana) (Human - ",{"title":"Qeynos"},")"],"steps":[{"parts":["Bandit Sashes to Chesgard in the paladin guild."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["Give 2 gold to Lashun Novashine and/or 2 bone chips to raise Priests of Life faction."],"steps":[]}]},{"parts":[{"title":"Priests of Marr"}," & ",{"title":"Knights of Truth"}," (Mithaniel Marr) (Human - ",{"title":"Freeport"},")"],"steps":[{"parts":["A way to raise faction with the Priests of Marr is to give ",{"title":"Bottle of Milk","label":"bottles of milk"}," to Mojak Hikspin, who fishes by the lake in West Commonlands. Giving Mojax milk will spawn a npc named Duggin Scumper, a thief. Kill Duggin and return the note to ",{"title":"Eestyana Naestra"}," in the Hall of Truth in North Freeport. If you dont want to run back and forth from WC to NFP, you can just keep giving milk to Mojax. You can give him up to 4 individual bottles (one in each trade slot) at a time."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["Kill Orcs for Knights of Truth faction in the common lands or assist people who are killing orcs."],"steps":[]}]},{"parts":[{"title":"Temple Of Sol Ro"}," (",{"title":"The Temple of Solusek Ro"},")"],"steps":[{"parts":["The best way to raise Temple of Sol Ro faction is to seek out Rathmana in South Ro (NW corner of zone), and give him 30 gold at at time (it must be 30 gold or 3 platinum, both work)."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["Alternatively, if you're a dervish hunter, you can turn in 4 dervish rings to Ortallius, the orc who is next to Rathmana."],"steps":[]},{"parts":["If you hang around Mistmoore a lot, you can raise faction there if you camp in the graveyard. There is a ",{"title":"Flower"}," that spawns in the crypt, which you can give to an outcast Shadowman named ",{"title":"Ssynthi"},", who sits behind the crypt building. Be careful of the invisible pit traps inside the crypt! You simply go to the Graveyard in MM. In the tomb you will see a bag, pick it up. You'll find a flower on your cursor. Go behind the Tomb and there is an outcast Shadowed Man named Synthi there, give her the flower. Rinse and repeat. The flower spawns every 1 minute. When Synthi cons amiable to you, your faction is high enough."],"steps":[]}]}],"card":{"title":"Armor of Ro Quests","lines":["Minimum Level: 30+","Classes: Paladin","Related Zones: Various","Related NPCs: Priestess Ghalea, a sand giant, an ancille cook"]},"links":["Temple of Solusek Ro","Lord Searfire","Paladin","Priestess Ghalea","A sand giant","An ancille cook","The Temple of Solusek Ro","Rathe Mountains","A Bar of Ronium","Helm of Ro","Breastplate of Ro","Vambraces of Ro","Bracer of Ro","Gauntlets of Ro","Greaves of Ro","Boots of Ro","Mold of Ro Boots","Kilij Plans","Mold of Ro Bracer","Deepwater Goblin Net","Mold of Ro Breastplate","Dark Cauldron","Mold of Ro Gauntlets","A Locket","Mold of Ro Greaves","Nightfall Giant's Head","Mold of Ro Helm","Cyclops Skull","Mold of Ro Vambrace","Rotten Shark Meat","Clerics of Underfoot","Sandgiant Husam","Southern Desert of Ro","Kazon Stormhammer","Miners Guild 249","Deepwater Knights","A goblin net master","Lake Rathe","Clockwork Gnome","Heretics","Abigail","Clerics of Tunare","Mistmoore Castle","Priests of Marr","Sentry Alechin","A werewolf","Southern Karana","Knights of Truth","A nightfall giant","West Commonlands","Knights of Thunder","An undead cyclops","Priests of Life","A plague shark","Erud's Crossing","Sol Cauldron","Bar of Ronium","Enchanted Platinum Bar","Melatite","Mistmoore Granite","Sand of Ro","Soil of Underfoot","Skill Blacksmithing","Enchant Platinum","Platinum Bar","Solusek's Eye","Gnome","Mistmoore","Cazel","Northern Desert of Ro","Oasis of Marr","Kaladim","Fairy Dust","SoulFire","Erudin","Elial Brook","Aglthin Dasmore","Noclin Saah","Zombie Flesh Quest","The Estate of Unrest","Odus Pearls","Felwithe","Qeynos","Freeport","Bottle of Milk","Eestyana Naestra","Temple Of Sol Ro","Flower","Ssynthi"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Nicholas","text":"Greetings, friend. I am the keeper of the [Boots of Ro]. Please rest here with us in our camp of righteousness. No harm can come to you while we paladins keep watch."},{"npc":"Nicholas","text":"If you desire the mold needed for smithin the Boots of Ro, then first, you shall prove your power. I have long sought an ancient holy weapon called the brazen brass kilij. I have heard rumors of detailed plans on how to make it, coming from Faydwer. Seek out the Kilij plans. Bring them to me and you shall have the mold."},{"npc":"David","text":"I, the keeper of the [Bracers of Ro], welcome you. Come and rest within our camp. You have nothing to fear while such righteous might is gathered."},{"npc":"David","text":"When you can swim the waters of Rathe and return two goblin nets from the elusive goblin net masters. then you will be rewarded the bracer mold."},{"npc":"Abigail","text":"The Breastplate of Ro mold will be awarded to you. First, you must perform a test of strength. Go to Faydwer. There you shall seek out and destroy the Tier'Dal who carry the dark cauldrons!! They have been venturing into our lands and capturing many Koada'Dal and Fier'Dal for cooking purposes! Bring me two of their dark cauldrons."},{"npc":"Sentry Joanna","text":"Love and passion to you. my friend. Seek you the [Gauntlets of Ro]? If not, then I offer you the safety of this camp."},{"npc":"Sentry Joanna","text":"I will give you the mold. but first you will complete a task in the name of Erollisi Marr. My fellow Sentry. Alechin. was bitten by a wolf while he journeyed to Qeynos. He now turns into a werewolf at night. forced to kill innocent travelers. Go toward Qeynos. Release him from life and his curse and return his locket to me."},{"npc":"Sentry Joanna","text":"Thank you my friend. It is good to see him free at last. I shall miss him. Here now is the mold of gauntlets as promised. Go and speak with Thomas about [Lord Searfire]."},{"npc":"Elisabeth","text":"Go to the countryside of Freeport. There, you shall seek out any nightfall giants. They have terrorized the countryside for too long. They have protection from common weapons. Rely on magic. I failed in tracking them down. You shall succeed and when return any single head to me. you shall be awarded the mold for the greaves."},{"npc":"Thomas","text":"Welcome to our camp. We are paladins gathered from many lands. We have been called to this land by our deities. Ours is a crusade or righteousness. Have you happened upon us by chance or do you [seek the sacred molds]?"},{"npc":"Thomas","text":"Many of us carry the sacred molds of the holy paladin armor. We will release it only to those who have proven themselves to each of our deities. If you seek it, speak up!! Tell us which part you seek. I carry the secret of the [Helm of Ro]. The others carry those of vambraces, breastplates, bracers, gauntlets, greaves and boots of Ro."},{"npc":"Thomas","text":"To receive the mold of the Helm of Ro you must first demonstrate your strength. Go to the plains of thunder. There you shall hunt down the most vile creatures I have ever encounterd. Seek the undead cyclopes. I have spied them in the most dangerous portions of my realm. Fetch me two of their skulls."},{"npc":"Thomas","text":"You have proven yourself to Karana. I grant you the mold of the Ro Helm. May the winds of Karana blow in your favor. Now you must seek out [Lord Searfire] and ask him for [ronium] to complete the second and only other component needed to be fashioned by a master blacksmith."},{"npc":"Marianna","text":"Rodcet Nife welcomes you into our noble camp. I am the keeper of the [Vambraces of Ro]."},{"npc":"Marianna","text":"The mold will be offered to you when you have performed a task for the Temple of Life. The oceans near our home are host to a plague.. the plague sharks!!. They have been infected with a deadly malady which has been turning up in Qeynos Hills. Kill the sharks and bring me two of their rotten shark portions as proof."},{"npc":"Lord Searfire","text":"You seek ronium. It is a fine blend of metals. I alone hold the secret of its formula. I, and I alone, can offer it to those who serve this temple. Do you wish a [bar of the alloy]?"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-10-26T04:16:09.647Z","outOfEra":false}
